--- answer ---
The bug was due to an off‑by‑one loop in `Resize` that evicted one extra entry when the new capacity was equal to or larger than the current number of items.

**Fix implemented**
- Adjusted the loop condition in `simplelru/lru.go` to iterate only `diff` times (`i < diff`) instead of `i <= diff`.

All tests now pass.

```go
// simplelru/lru.go
- for i := 0; i <= diff; i++ {
+ for i := 0; i < diff; i++ {
```

This ensures `Resize` correctly retains all entries when the capacity is not reduced.